{% comment %}
  Ingredient spotlight button icons, extracted from Santosh's "KCC Ingredient Buttons.svg"
  composite file (9 circle buttons laid out in a row). Each button in that file is a
  <g> containing an outline ellipse (the circle border, recreated in CSS instead of here)
  plus a sibling <g> with the actual glyph artwork.

  Extraction method: loaded the composite file in a headless browser, located each
  button by the x-offset in its ellipse's transform, then measured the glyph group's
  tight bounding box. getBBox() on a transformed <g> returns the box in the group's own
  *pre-transform* local space -- reusing that box directly as a viewBox while keeping the
  group's transform attribute intact renders blank (the transform then applies a second
  time and throws the content miles outside the viewBox). Fixed by manually transforming
  the local bbox's four corners through the group's own consolidated matrix and taking
  the enclosing box of those transformed corners -- that's the box the group actually
  occupies in its parent's coordinate system, which is what a fresh standalone viewBox
  needs. Fill was hardcoded to the brand orange (rgb(205,100,62)) throughout the source
  file; replaced with currentColor so these inherit color the same way the icon-or-image
  snippet's fallback glyphs already do.

  Of the 9 buttons in the source file, 3 (index 1, 4, 6) contain no visible artwork --
  just the outline circle, no path or a fully-transparent masked image. Only the other 6
  are defined below; sections/ingredient-spotlight.liquid falls back to the theme's icon
  picker (via icon-or-image) for any index with no case here.

  Assigned to spice blocks in the order the buttons appear in the source file (left to
  right = block_order position 0 to 8). Index 0 was a confident match for Ginger --
  it's the one button drawn as detailed outline/line-art (27 paths of wrinkle and vein
  detail) matching the line-art style of Santosh's reference screenshot's ginger
  illustration, everything else in the file is solid-fill. The other 5 were not
  independently identifiable as specific spices from path data alone, so they're applied
  in sequence (cinnamon, cloves, fennel, coffee, tea) rather than guessed at -- flagged
  to Santosh to confirm/reassign.
{% endcomment %}

{%- case index -%}
  {%- when 0 -%}
    {%- comment -%} Ginger (root, line-art detail) {%- endcomment -%}
